h>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Dragoon\"><img alt=\"Delusory Dragoon\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fleeting Flash\"><img alt=\"Fleeting Flash\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest?cb=20100712153022\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Summon\"><img alt=\"Summon\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Summonstone.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Summonstone.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20100712153022\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>A Jump Chain at C2 or a Multichain at C3 will chain all enemies here. I had neither so I killed the enemy at D2 and then moved there and used a Round Chain. The enemies here are a Delusory Dragoon with Demon Wall as a summon, Fallacious Tree with Typhon, Fleeting Flash with Odin, another Fleeting Flash with nothing, and the Expert Battle Piece, an Imitation Despot. \n</p><p>The Tree is a new enemy type, an Exdeath manikin. It uses Sword Dance, pausing for a second or two before sweeping the sword, and Hurricane, surrounding itself in a whirlwind. Its HP attack is Delta Attack, where it creates a field of energy and fires a long-range blast of light from the center. The crest deflects attacks like a block so wait for the blast to fire and die down before countering. The Tree will be encountered from now on of course, and it's Battlegen items can be used to trade for the Heart's Ease, which boosts your Bravery a little every time you block an attack, and isn't much worth it.\n</p><p>The Imitation Despot is a tough one. He has a Hyper Ring, Guardian Ring, and boosters that all trigger at full HP, so land an HP attack first thing to deactivate them and rob him of his considerable power boost. He has Landmine, Mine, Bombard, Light Crest, Thunder Crest, the ground and aerial versions of Flare, Starfall, good equipment, and the Carbuncle Summon. I recommend using your Maser Eye to knock off half his HP, which is around the 2500 area, give or take a couple hundred.\n</p><p>The summonstone is Shiva, who has an amusing scene of teasing Firion when she senses him. She appears when the opponent's Bravery hits 0 and locks it so it can't increase. The auto version is useless for the moment, the only time an opponent's Bravery will hit 0 is if they're in the middle of getting attacked and are gonna get Broken, and Shiva doesn't stop the Bravery regen, or they just landed an HP attack, and that shouldn't be happening since enemies are still dumb as a post so far. The chest has a Black Dragon Spear, a powerful exclusive weapon for Kain. Also at this point, Kain hit Level 8 and learned Sky Rave. He moves forward a bit and dives down, drilling the opponent into the ground. It and its cousin move, Rising Drive, are meant to be used for combos because Sky Rave does a huge amount of Bravery damage the longer Kain drives them into the ground, so you want an Assist to get the opponent stunned at the top of the arena. But if you want to try it out, run up a pillar in the World of Darkness, block the opponent when they dash towards you, then let loose and watch the fun.\n</p><p>As we exit the gateway Firion asks why Kain is alone, and he dodges the question, musing though that they're doing well fighting the manikins so far, so it's not yet time to take out Firion when he can still help clear the nearby gateways.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"The_Tree.27s_Pursuit\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Tree's_Pursuit\">The Tree's Pursuit</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Tree&#39;s Pursuit\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_6?action=edit&amp;section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Tree&#39;s Pursuit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the overworld map now, make a left and open the chest for a Pink Tail. On the shoreline to the left is a Fallacious Tree, it has Delta Attack again but is otherwise unremarkable. The Trees are easy to get the drop on on the overworld because their attack to initiate battle is Sword Dance, which is amazingly slow and easy to avoid. The chest beyond him has a KP Gambler, we're going to save it for the next chapter because we want to use it to chain as many enemies as possible and Kain can't get any more than four in the remaining gateways. The chest on the island has the Jump skill, which lets us leap over an enemy piece in a gateway to land behind them. We'll have a use for it too. The Counterfeit Wraith here has a new move, Long-Range Particle Beam, which creates a line of energy orbs that run along the ground firing lasers high into the air, fairly simple to dodge. On the hill behind it with the ruined castle is a chest with 1000 gil.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-nam