peof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fallacious Tree\"><img alt=\"Fallacious Tree\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"500 gil\"><img alt=\"500 gil\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest?cb=20110126024837\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist - Firion\"><img alt=\"Assist - Firion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff2 Fir1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20110126024837\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The enemies here are at first unremarkable, but they do have a new trick. The line-up is a Fleeting Flash, Idle Sky Pirate, Transient Gunner and Fallacious Tree. All of them except the Gunner have an accessory line-up of an Attractorb, Dragonfly Orb, Pearl Necklace, and six Break boosters. Thus once you break them, they get more than an 11x booster, greatly increasing the range at which they absorb EX Force and how much they get from it. As a result their gauge will charge surprisingly fast. They also have summons, Odin for the Flash and Sky Pirate, Typhon for the Tree. The Gunner is the weakest but has a midair Pummel that goes off pretty quick, so be ready to block it, it won't hurt much but on principle, not to mention it negates the AP chance. Also it may just be me, but the Idle Sky Pirate was a bit smarter than I expected, got in a few hits on me.\n</p><p>Use the Jump skill to jump over the enemy at D4 and chain all four enemies without skills, and use that Assist Charge we got earlier for an advantage on their haxxor EX powers, as well as to help with their high HP. The chests have 500 gil and a Pebble for us.\n</p><p>On the overworld now, shatter the stone and grind to the island, depending on where it is when you land the Fallacious Tree may attack as soon as you land so be ready to dodge if so. The arena is new, Planet's Core, we can Battlegen the Materia here. The Materia is the last component, along with Reaper's Dreams and Gunner's Dreams, for the Zephyr Cloak, we don't need it but something of note. Now just gather the orbs of the dead and approach the moogle.\n</p><p>The summons can mostly be passed up, though if you must buy one go for Carbuncle. For weapons, we can still afford the big 200 KP ones. I would say buy the Snowscepter, the character in the next storyline can't use weapons most of the rest can but she can use Staves, so the Snowscepter will do well for her, and continue to be handy in later storylines for spellcasters that can't use guns or swords like the rest of the cast. The Grounded and Aerial boosters are good, they can be annoying since you have to stay on the ground or in the air, but they have their uses. I'll pass them up though since we don't really need boosters urgently yet. I also bought several more Rosetta Stones, six, leaving me with 57 KP. I only used one of them for Kain though. Now just buy a Multichain and head into the gateway now.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Exdeath\"><img alt=\"Exdeath\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest?cb=20110126024837\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist - Firion\"><img alt=\"Assist - Firion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff2 Fir1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20110126024837\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Dragoon\"><img alt=\"Delusory Dragoon\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Girl\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Girl\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Yellow Drop\"><img alt=\"Yellow Drop\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>A Multichain at E4 is the way to get them all here. The line-up is a Delusory Dragoon, Transient Gunner, Phantasmal Girl and Idle Sky Pirate. The Gunner and Sky Pirate have the same EX Mode accessories as the enemies in the last gateway, and the Gunner has Odin and the Sky Pirate has Typhon. The Girl is the Strange Battle Piece and has a Bravery boost and the Giant of Babil summon with Holy Combo-Ultima. Nothing new here, in short.\n</p><p>During this round of fighting Kain learned Celestial Shooter at Level 13. It's an upwards lunge aerial Bravery attack, and its upward follow-up slam the opponent into the ceiling. It's of limited use in my opinion, I prefer to slam opponents into the ground, knocking them higher puts them out of reach more often than not. But the initial strike is good as an upward leap so it's not useless. I also got the \"Hard Habit to Break\" accomplishment, getting me the pretty useless Desert Boots. The chest has a Yellow Drop which boosts Luck by 1, totally useless since the Pink Tail gives +4, among many other trade items.\n</p><p>Once the enemies are taken out approach the end piece and Kain will send Firion ahead, then strike him down as he walks away. I'm not sure why part of this scene is only text and the rest is a full cutscene, presumably its so you don't see Kain strike him down, but why, we see other people get attacked. Anyway as Firion lies wounded, Exdeath appears to taunt us, but Kain of course isn't about to let him find out where he's taking Firion and the rest of his allies. So, only one thing to do.\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Exdeath_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Exdeath (Dissidia PSP)\">Exdeath</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/63/Exdeath_Render.png/revision/latest?cb=20110519024644\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Exdeath Render\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"155\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Exdeath Render.png\" data-image-key=\"Exdeath_Render.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/63/Exdeath_Render.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110519024644\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">2,725\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">18\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">286\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Reverse Polarity, Turn Guard, Omni Block, Hurricane, Sword Dance\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Delta Attack, Almagest, Grand Cross\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Hecatoncheir\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">3/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>I love Kain's one-liner. \"So, you offer your life in exchange for theirs?\" \"Of course not. I offer yours.\" Exdeath is an opponent entirely different from any other up until now due to a radically different fighting style, even the Fallacious Trees haven't tapped into his true power yet. First, he has the smartest accessory set-up of any opponent so far. He has Pre-Assist and Assist Gauge Empty, and since he doesn't have an Assist at all they'll be active the entire match for an instant 2.1 boost. Then, he has After Summon, which will tack on another 1.3 once he calls his summon for 2.7 during the rest of the match, and finally he has a booster that triggers when his Bravery is its base value or lower for another 1.3, leading to a potential 3.5x booster. And what is getting boosted? Attractorb and Pearl Necklace to help him charge up the EX Gauge, and unlike the Manikins, he's going to live long enough to potentially do it. And this time of course, no Firion Assist anymore to help you stop him. His summon, Hecatoncheir, is usually called when he's at low Bravery, it'll sap the Bravery pool to 0 so you get no bonus for Breaking him. Annoying, but it only works once, after the first time Break is inflicted the Bravery pool resets like normal.\n</p><p>Now, Exdeath's manikins have had slow, easy to avoid or block attacks. This is because Exdeath's true power isn't in offense, it's defense. When he blocks an attack using a Guard or Block move, he can instantly use Sword Dance, Vacuum Wave or Hurricane, and they execute faster, and have a higher critical hit rate since you got blocked while he attacked. Turn Guard is a glow red and orange barrier where Exdeath turns to keep defending, you need to use a guard-crushing attack, fortunately all of Kain's HP attacks are such. Omni Block blocks <i>anything</i>, everything you throw at him, and it's a momentary instant-activation block, fortunately the AI sucks at using it. Reverse Polarity sends out a circle of energy that Exdeath can instantly teleport to when he chooses, and if he teleports on top of you you're damaged, <i>and</i> he can use an attack immediately, so you're likely to get knocked into the air and come back down into the blast from Delta Attack, or get caught in a Hurricane. And his new HP attacks, Almagest has him move towards you in a field of energy and explode, and he can stop it in the middle of execution to block your attack, and Grand Cross summons orbs of darkness to spin and converge on you.\n</p><p>All in all, Exdeath is surprisingly the strongest boss yet, especially if you're a new player and don't know the quirks of his playstyle and how to counter him. There is no way to stop his Omni Block, it comes out way too fast for you to know he's even preparing it, and when he lands it you are going to feel pain. If he uses Almgaest, he can block you if you try to attack him and you will feel pain. If he hits you with Reverse Polarity, you are <i>probably</i> going to feel pain. The main thing to watch for is Reverse Polarity, it always fires straight at you, do a neutral dodge and Exdeath will teleport right in front of you, you'll avoid damage and can attack him before he recovers from the teleportation. And if he does hit you with it, use Aerial Recovery quickly so you don't fall back down into his next attack. \n</p><p>The best opening you can ask for besides Reverse Polarity is Hurricane, make sure you have enough distance from him to get it off safety and chuck a Gungnir in his face. He <i>might</i> stop Hurricane by Omni Blocking and pain is soon to follow, but it's a risk you'll have to take because there's not much you can do to stop him. You can also try to hit as he fires out Reverse Polarity, but likely he'll teleport out of the way and laugh in your face. What stops Exdeath from just curb-stomping you is his AI again, the AI is good at using him, but not <i>too</i> good. Fake him out by attacking when he's nowhere near you and this will bait him into Reverse Polarity, dodge and counter as described. And if he Omni Blocks but mistimes it, the ending lag of it is a perfect opening. Overall just don't be too aggressive or he'll make you pay for it, be cautious and wait for your chance to strike when he gives you an opening.\n</p><p>I never talked about Kain's EX Mode but I like finishing off bosses with EX Bursts, so this is the first time I've gotten into EX Mode actually. Kain gets a special attack called Lancet by pressing R and Square, it has a second's long charge time and causes a giant blade of energy to impale the opponent from below. The attack will not only do HP damage, but Kain is healed the HP he inflicted. Furthermore, Lancet will recharge to base Bravery very quickly after it hits, and you can press Triangle to dash at the opponent like Kain's melee moves. His EX Burst has you rapidly tap a button to build up a power meter, and the button turns over and changes twice as he jumps, very easy to get right. Appropriately Exdeath is very vulnerable to Lancet when using Delta Attack or Hurricane.\n</p><p>In the aftermath Exdeath retreats, but leaves Kain a parting gift, a few Delusory Manikins to play with. Kain is unimpressed and so am I, we've killed how many so far in the game, and he only brings out three? The tree vanishes and Kain once again gets some badass boasting. \"I'm about to teach you pathetic mockeries the difference between you, and a <i>real</i> man!\" \n</p><p>As always we unlock a Report for this, but it's just cutscenes again. Hit the PP Catalog and continue to Chapter 7.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</strong> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 12\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 14\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 15\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 16\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-8/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 17\">8</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-9/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 18\">9</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-10/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 19\">10</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 20\">Epilogue Part 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 21\">Part 2</a><hr />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">Next page</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b><a href=\"https://final